-- title:
--   Edge points lie on consecutive components of the chain
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$, a Deligne–Rapoport model package $\mathfrak{X}$ for $p$, a discrete valuation domain $O$ whose maximal ideal is generated by the image of $p$, an algebraically closed field $\kappa$ of characteristic $p$, and a ring homomorphism $\mathrm{toκ} : O \to \kappa$. Assume the site hypotheses [`V3Asm.SiteHyps`](def/ModularCurve_ResolvedModelSite.html#L267): finiteness of the node set $\mathrm{Node}\,p\,\mathfrak{X}\,\kappa = \mathrm{pullback}(\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{compInf}\,\kappa,\ \mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{compZero}\,\kappa)$, the existence of oriented crossing charts, the étale neighbourhood data, injectivity of $n \mapsto \mathrm{xpt}\,n$ and closedness of each point $\mathrm{xpt}\,n$, together with the model hypotheses; assume further that each section $\xi_j$ lies in the open set $\mathrm{X0}$ of the chart input $C$, i.e. in the complement of the union of the crossing points. Let $Y$ be the glued scheme, $\mathrm{width} = C.\mathrm{thick}$, and let $\mathrm{comp}$ be the resulting family of ideal sheaf data on $Y$ indexed by the components $\mathrm{X0MqComponents}(\mathrm{width})$. Then for every node $n$ and every $d \in \mathrm{Fin}(\mathrm{width}\,n)$ the point $\mathrm{edgePt}\,n\,d$ of $Y$ lies in the intersection of the supports, as subsets of $Y$, of $\mathrm{comp}(\mathrm{chainPos}\,\mathrm{width}\,n\,d)$ and $\mathrm{comp}(\mathrm{chainPos}\,\mathrm{width}\,n\,(d+1))$, where $\mathrm{chainPos}$ sends $0$ to the first end component $\mathrm{inl}\,0$, an index $0 < d < \mathrm{width}\,n$ to the interior component $\mathrm{inr}\,\langle n, d-1\rangle$ of the chain at $n$, and any index $\ge \mathrm{width}\,n$ to the second end component $\mathrm{inl}\,1$.
--
--   This records the incidence pattern of the special fibre of the resolved model: the $d$-th edge point of the chain inserted at a crossing $n$ lies on both the $d$-th and the $(d+1)$-st component of that chain, the two extreme positions being the components coming from the two ends ($\mathrm{compInf}$ and $\mathrm{compZero}$ in the Deligne–Rapoport description). It is one of the incidence conditions verified in [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.exists_dRResolvedModelPackageV4_and_dRResolvedModelCharts`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.exists_dRResolvedModelPackageV4_and_dRResolvedModelCharts), which produces a resolved Deligne–Rapoport model package together with its crossing charts.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_V3Asm_edgePt_mem.lean

